  "text": "In September of 2013 we kept returning to the machinery of funding. 39 of us said \"a government shutdown\"; 38 reached for \"a continuing resolution,\" 34 for \"the continuing resolution.\" 33 of us named the \"medical device tax.\" 30 of us spoke of keeping \"the government open.\" On September 11, 30 of us said \"the 12th anniversary of,\" 33 \"12th anniversary of.\" 31 of us invoked \"members of congress.\" The shutdown language crested on September 30, at the close of the month; the device tax the day before. We report this without comment: the words arriving together, dozens of us at a time. The record from this era is not thin. It is a chorus we entered as one.",
